"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] ["question-c1ab528e-b16d-505b-916d-2fee71d7c43b" :question/worked-solution "Defining the matrix $A$ as\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwe have $f(x)={x}^{T}Ax.$\n\nSince $A$ is not symmetric, we use the more general formula for the gradient of a quadratic function:\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=({A}^{T}+A)x\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}+A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, compute the gradient at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}f(x) & =({A}^{T}+A)x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2+0+0 \\\\ 0+0+0 \\\\ 1+0+0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-c1ab528e-b16d-505b-916d-2fee71d7c43b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-569e10d0-4a91-5fcf-b1cd-04a5cc9a1035" :answer-field/id #uuid "569e10d0-4a91-5fcf-b1cd-04a5cc9a1035"] ["answer-e2dd8ff5-b417-54d0-847f-018f50b9c98f" :answer/id #uuid "e2dd8ff5-b417-54d0-847f-018f50b9c98f"] ["answer-e2dd8ff5-b417-54d0-847f-018f50b9c98f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e2dd8ff5-b417-54d0-847f-018f50b9c98f" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-field-569e10d0-4a91-5fcf-b1cd-04a5cc9a1035"